# Checks daily, after NSE market close, whether needrestart still has mysqld
# flagged for a restart (from an unattended-upgrades libc/security patch
# earlier that day) and restarts it gracefully in this low-traffic window if
# so. See ops/needrestart/ for the config that stops needrestart from
# restarting mysql automatically/silently.
#
# 10:20 UTC = 15:50 IST. This ran at 10:05 UTC (15:35 IST) until 2026-08-11,
# which was safely past the old 15:30 close - but NSE now trades to 15:41,
# so that slot had become SIX MINUTES BEFORE the close, i.e. a MySQL restart
# in the middle of live ingest. Any future change to the session window has
# to be checked against this line.
#
# Points at ops/scripts/, not scripts/. There is an UNTRACKED copy of this
# script at /opt/option-decode/scripts/mysql-safe-restart.sh on the host
# which this cron used to run - so every edit to the tracked ops/scripts/
# copy was landing somewhere cron never looked. Same class of bug as the
# logrotate paths. The untracked copy is now unreferenced; don't edit it.
20 10 * * * root /opt/option-decode/ops/scripts/mysql-safe-restart.sh
